tation-type="display-unstructured">Sherif MM (1994) First dorsal metacarpal artery flap in hand reconstruction. II. Clinical application. J Hand Surg 19A:26&#x02013;31 </citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eski</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nisanci</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sengezer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Correction of thumb deformities after burn: Versatility of first dorsal metacarpal artery flap</article-title><source>Burn</source><year>2007</year><volume>33</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>65</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.burns.2006.04.030</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eski M, Nisanci M, Sengezer M (2007) Correction of thumb deformities after burn: Versatility of first dorsal metacarpal artery flap. Burn 33(1):65&#x02013;71 </citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pelissier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Casoli</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Bakhach</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Baudet</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reverse dorsal digital and metacarpal flaps: a review of 27 cases</article-title><source>Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>1999</year><volume>103</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>165</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006534-199901000-00025</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pelissier P, Casoli V, Bakhach J, Martin D, Baudet J (1999) Reverse dorsal digital and metacarpal flaps: a review of 27 cases. Plast Reconstr Surg 103(1):159&#x02013;165 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9915177</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>El Khatib</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical experiences with the extended first dorsal metacarpal artery island flap for thumb reconstruction</article-title><source>J Hand Surg [Am]</source><year>1998</year><volume>23</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>647</fpage><lpage>652</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0363-5023(98)80050-6</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">El Khatib HA (1998) Clinical experiences with the extended first dorsal metacarpal artery island flap for thumb reconstruction. J Hand Surg [Am] 23(4):647&#x02013;652 </citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yoshinori</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sensory function of the neurovascular island flap in thumb reconstruction: comparison of original and modified procedures</article-title><source>J Hand Surg [Am]</source><year>2000</year><volume>25A</volume><fpage>637</fpage><lpage>643</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Yoshinori O (2000) Sensory function of the neurovascular island flap in thumb reconstruction: comparison of original and modified procedures. J Hand Surg [Am] 25A:637&#x02013;643 </citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tr&#x000e4;nkle</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sauerbier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Heitmann</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Germann</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Restoration of thumb sensibility with the innervated first dorsal metacarpal artery island flap</article-title><source>J Hand Surg [Am]</source><year>2003</year><volume>28</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>758</fpage><lpage>766</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0363-5023(03)00369-1</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Tr&#x000e4;nkle M, Sauerbier M, Heitmann C, Germann G (2003) Restoration of thumb sensibility with the innervated first dorsal metacarpal artery island flap. J Hand Surg [Am] 28(5):758&#x02013;766 </citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shun-Cheng</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Shao-Liang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tim-Mo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Chia-Jueng</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tian-Yeu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsian-Jenn</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sensate first dorsal metacarpal artery flap for resurfacing extensive pulp defects of the thumb</article-title><source>Ann Plast Surg</source><year>2004</year><volume>53</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>449</fpage><lpage>454</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.sap.0000137134.15728.dd</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Shun-Cheng C, Shao-Liang C, Tim-Mo C, Chia-Jueng C, Tian-Yeu C, Hsian-Jenn W (2004) Sensate first dorsal metacarpal artery flap for resurfacing extensive pulp defects of the thumb. Ann Plast Surg 53(5):449&#x02013;454 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15502460</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>